{"id":"R0007","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"T","E4":"F","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"U"},"primary":"E4","secondary":[],"reason":"Section III.B evaluates only federated learning training convergence and trained model detection rather than the collaborative inference module; Poster & Demo peer-review status also remains unverified.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"Abstract","present a working prototype of CIOFL on embedded","Describes a primary system prototype contribution."],["E2","PDF",2,"III.A Demo design","implemented CIOFL on four devices: two Jetson TX2","Evaluates a multi-node UAV swarm prototype using UAV-captured images."],["E3","PDF",2,"II.A Collaborative inference module","divide the large-scale model into multiple submodels and","Partitions Faster-RCNN across multiple nodes for collaborative inference labeling."],["E4","PDF",2,"III.B Results","recorded the global loss and mAP for 20","Evaluates only FL training schemes (global loss, mAP, qualitative FL output) without evaluating collaborative inference execution or partitioning."],["E5","PDF",1,"Header","2022 IEEE 19th International Conference on Mobile Ad","2022 proceedings year falls wholly within 2021-01-01 to 2026-11-26."],["E6","PDF",1,"Abstract","Federated learning (FL) has great potential in visual","Full 2-page report is written in English."],["E7","PDF",1,"Abstract","In this demonstration, we present a working prototype","Self-identified demonstration in Poster & Demo track; official CFP subpage was inaccessible so peer-review status remains unverified."],["E7","https://sites.google.com/view/ieee-mass-2022",0,"Updates","Posters and Demos submission deadline is extended","Confirms separate Posters and Demos track without stating its peer-review policy on the accessible main page."]]}
{"id":"R0023","access":"READ","decision":"AWAITING_CLASSIFICATION","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"T","E4":"T","E5":"U","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"","secondary":[],"reason":"Cutoff-year 2026 IEEE proceedings report lacks a verified authoritative online release date for DOI 10.1109/ACDSA67686.2026.11467610.","study_link_note":"Shares identical EASA three-tier design, 30-node testbed (p. 4), quantitative comparison values (p. 4 Table II), fault-tolerance table (p. 6 Table III), and drone swarm case study (p. 6 Section V.E) with R0027 (DOI 10.1109/ICASS69550.2026.11547499) despite disjoint authors and venue; distinct DOI record retained as unresolved linkage lead.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"III.A An architectural overview","Edge Agentic Systems Architecture (EASA) is a layered","Presents a primary multi-tier decentralized edge AI architecture."],["E2","PDF",6,"V.E Useful Case Studies","Drone Swarm Coordination enhanced formation consistency by 12%","Evaluates multi-agent drone swarm coordination on a 30-node edge testbed."],["E3","PDF",5,"V.C Energy-Latency Tradeoff","allocates compute between local inference and neighbor-assisted reasoning","Distributes TinyML neural inference and peer-assisted reasoning across edge agents."],["E4","PDF",4,"V. Results and Quantitative Analysis","empirically tested across 50 distinct experimental runs","Reports experimental and simulation evaluation across baselines, scalability, faults, and drone swarm case study."],["E5","PDF",1,"Header","5-7 February 2026, Boracay Island-Philippines","Only conference event dates and 2026 copyright appear; exact online publication date for this DOI was not directly verified."],["E6","PDF",1,"Abstract","EASA provides a decentralised and modular framework for","Full 6-page report is written in English."],["E7","https://www.acdsa.org/2026/",0,"Welcome To ACDSA 2026","All paper submissions will be peer reviewed and","Official ACDSA 2026 website confirms peer review; PDF provides full method and evaluation."]]}
