eview and TPC decisions; PDF provides full method and evaluation."]]}
{"id":"R0028","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"F","E5":"U","E6":"T","E7":"U"},"primary":"E3","secondary":["E4"],"reason":"Implements closed-loop dataset annotation/training and standalone onboard YOLO11s detection without a formulated or evaluated collaborative DNN inference method; 2026 online release date and workshop peer-review policy also remain unverified.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"Abstract","presents a distributed, link-aware architecture for automated dataset","Presents a primary system architecture and field experiment."],["E2","PDF",4,"V. Experiment Setup","three DJI Matrice 350 RTK UAVs, each equipped","Uses a multi-UAV FANET architecture and three UAVs in field acquisition missions."],["E3","PDF",3,"II.B Model Training and real-time inference","fine-tune a lightweight detector, specifically a YOLO11 Small","Checked Sections II, III, V, VI: edge YOLOE annotates training data and trained YOLO11s runs standalone onboard without a formulated collaborative inference algorithm."],["E3","PDF",6,"VI. Numerical Results","deployed in an operational FANET for Aerial Inference","Actual deployment runs standalone YOLO11s on one Raspberry Pi 5 mounted on a single DJI Matrice 350 RTK."],["E4","PDF",5,"VI. Numerical Results","reports the evolution of the main training losses","Checked Sections V–VI: evaluates SSIM frame reduction, YOLO11s training losses, and test-set/single-device detection rather than collaborative inference."],["E4","PDF",4,"V. Experiment Setup","Controlled bandwidth-stress experiments were not performed in this","Confirms link-aware and multi-UAV service-chain inference evaluation was not conducted."],["E5","PDF",1,"Header","2026 IEEE 12th International Conference on Network Softwarization","Cutoff-year 2026 copyright only; exact online release date for DOI 10.1109/NETSOFT70012.2026.11603504 was not verified."],["E6","PDF",1,"Abstract","creation of high-quality labeled datasets for training machine","Full 7-page report is written in English."],["E7","https://sites.google.com/view/ens2026/",0,"Paper Submission","included in the IEEE NetSoft 2026 Proceedings and","Official ENS 2026 homepage lists TPC chairs and IEEE Xplore publication but CFP subpage was inaccessible to verify explicit peer-review policy."]]}
{"id":"R0043","access":"READ","decision":"INCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"T","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"","secondary":[],"reason":"Meets all E1–E7 criteria as a peer-reviewed 2023 IEEE conference paper evaluating fine-grained multi-UAV collaborative DNN inference partitioning and offloading.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"Abstract","proposed DNN inference acceleration (DIA), an approach based","Proposes original DIA-FP partitioning and DIA-O offloading algorithms."],["E2","PDF",2,"II. System Model","dedicated computing UAVs equipped with server are regarded","Models and simulates multiple user UAVs (30) and server UAVs (6) in maritime SAR."],["E3","PDF",4,"III.B Offloading Strategy Based on DIA-O","offload fine-grained partitioned DNN tasks to multiple server","Partitions DNN fusion blocks across multiple computing UAV server nodes for collaborative inference."],["E4","PDF",5,"IV.A Simulation Setup","Four well-known DNN models are employed as benchmarks","Evaluates DIA total inference time across NiN, VGG16, AlexNet, and ResNet18 against three baselines."],["E5","PDF",1,"Header","2023 International Conference on Ubiquitous Communication (Ucom)","2023 proceedings year falls wholly within 2021-01-01 to 2026-11-26."],["E6","PDF",1,"Abstract","bring great advantages to maritime search and rescue","Full 6-page report is written in English."],["E7","https://easychair.org/cfp/Ucom2023",0,"Publication","The accepted papers passed through the peer-reviewed process","Official Ucom 2023 CFP confirms peer-reviewed IEEE proceedings; PDF provides full method and evaluation."]]}
{"id":"R0058","access":"READ","decision":"INCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"T","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"","secondary":[],"reason":"Meets all E1–E7 criteria as a peer-reviewed journal article published online 2025-12-06 evaluating distributed auction-based multi-UAV DNN inference offloading.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"Abstract","propose an adaptive AI inference offloading framework tailored","Proposes original DADAO distributed auction framework with theoretical proofs and simulations."],["E2","PDF",19,"6.1 Simulation settings","20-50 autonomous UAVs (default value: 25) to perform","Evaluates 20–50 autonomous UAVs with 5–10 edge servers."],["E3","PDF",19,"6.1 Simulation settings","Each UAV generates one DNN inference task per","Explicitly optimizes multi-UAV to edge-server DNN inference offloading assignment and compute allocation."],["E4","PDF",19,"6.1 Simulation settings","adopt ResNet-18 as the deep neural network (DNN)","Evaluates ResNet-18/CIFAR-10 inference accuracy, latency, mobility task success rate, and auction truthfulness against four baselines."],["E5","PDF",1,"Publication dates","Accepted 21 October 2025 Published 6 December 2025","Authoritative online publication date 2025-12-06 on physical page 1 is within 2021-01-01 to 2026-11-26."],["E6","PDF",1,"Abstract","Unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs) are increasingly utilized in","Full 25-page report is written in English."],["E7","https://www.worldscientific.com/page/jcsc/submission-guidelines",0,"Submission Guidelines","All submitted papers will be acknowledged and refereed","Official World Scientific JCSC guidelines confirm refereed peer review, matching Received/Accepted dates on PDF page 1."]]}
{"id":"R0064","access":"READ","decision":"INCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"T","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"","secondary":[],"reason":"Meets all E1–E7 criteria as a peer-reviewed journal article published online 2025-07-18 evaluating multi-UAV air-ground collaborative DNN inference via MAPPO-HA.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"Abstract","studies joint optimization for data sensing and computing","Proposes original air-ground collaborative inference formulation and MAPPO-HA algorithm."],["E2","PDF",11,"5.2.5 Performance analysis versus number of UAVs","in case of 2 and 3 UAVs, which","Evaluates multi-UAV surveillance with 2 and 3 UAVs assisted by 2 edge servers."],["E3","PDF",2,"1. Introduction","compressed DNN model is deployed at UAVs while","Collaboratively executes DNN inference across compressed UAV models and uncompressed ES models via joint offloading optimization."],["E4","PDF",9,"5.2.2 Impact of communication bandwidth","average inference delay and 95% confidence interval of","Evaluates inference delay, accuracy convergence, bandwidth, ES capacity, UAV count, and trajectories against six baselines."],["E5","PDF",1,"Article history","Accepted 7 July 2025 Available online 18 July 2025","Authoritative online publication date 2025-07-18 on physical page 1 is within 2021-01-01 to 2026-11-26."],["E6","PDF",1,"Abstract","Unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs) are increasingly used for","Full 13-page report is written in English."],["E7","PDF",1,"Article history","Received 22 March 2025; Received in revised form","Elsevier Computer Networks peer-reviewed journal article with revision/acceptance history, full method, and evaluation."]]}
{"id":"R0090","access":"READ","decision":"AWAITING_CLASSIFICATION","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"T","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"U"},"primary":"","secondary":[],"reason":"Official ICoEIT 2025 website does not explicitly confirm peer-review procedures for accepted papers.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"Abstract","conceptualizes AeroAgriNet as a swarm-enabled flying edge architecture","Presents a primary five-layer flying-edge swarm framework with evaluation."],["E2","PDF",5,"V.H Scalability under Load","increasing the number of UAVs from 1 to","Evaluates a UAV swarm scaled from 1 to 20 UAVs in simulation and ~30 drones in field testing."],["E3","PDF",3,"III.B Redundant Task Assignment and Fault Tolerance","local AI inference tasks are allocated to several","Allocates and reassigns onboard CNN/DL inference tasks across multiple UAVs with failover takeover."],["E4","PDF",5,"V.J Model Inference Time","Edge AI inference was benchmarked using lightweight CNNs","Evaluates CNN model inference time, latency, energy, scalability, and node-failure resilience against two baselines."],["E5","PDF",1,"Header","2025 International Conference on Engineering Innovations and Technologies","2025 proceedings year falls wholly within 2021-01-01 to 2026-11-26."],["E6","PDF",1,"Abstract","Existing agricultural practices encounter several challenges, including worker","Full 7-page report is written in English."],["E7","https://www.icoeit.org.lnctrishiraj.ac.in/Submission.html",0,"Submission Guidelines","Publication at IEEE Xplore is subject to IEEE's","Official submission page states IEEE Xplore submission policy but does not explicitly document peer review."]]}
{"id":"R0125","access":"READ","decision":"AWAITING_CLASSIFICATION","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"T","E4":"T","E5":"U","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"","secondary":[],"reason":"Cutoff-year 2026 IEEE proceedings report lacks a verified authoritative online release date for DOI 10.1109/SM69703.2026.11614110.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"Abstract","presents an UAV Extreme Edge Computing (UXEC) framework","Presents a primary distributed inference architecture and prototype."],["E2","PDF",1,"Abstract","distributes AI inference tasks across resource constrained UAVs","Models and evaluates a multi-UAV swarm across 1 to 6 simulated UAV workers."],["E3","PDF",2,"II.B Spatial Frame Decomposition","employs spatial frame decomposition to enable parallel processing","Partitions video frames across multiple UAV workers running YOLO11m in parallel with orchestrator result aggregation."],["E4","PDF",3,"IV.B Distributed Inference Scalability","presents throughput scaling with increasing worker count, where","Evaluates throughput scaling, latency CDF, heterogeneous threads, dynamic reallocation, detection quality, and overhead."],["E5","PDF",1,"Header","2026 International Conference on Smart Mobility (SM)","Cutoff-year 2026 copyright only; exact online publication date for DOI 10.1109/SM69703.2026.11614110 was not verified."],["E6","PDF",1,"Abstract","proliferation of Unmanned Aerial Vehicle (UAV) swarms for","Full 5-page report is written in English."],["E7","https://ieeesm.org/call-for-papers/",0,"Call for Papers","maintains a rigorous peer-review process, with an acceptance","Official SM 2026 CFP confirms peer review for technical papers, paired with TS5 technical-session listing on https://ieeesm.org/program/."],["E7","https://ieeesm.org/program/",0,"TS5: Technical Session #5","UAV Extreme Edge Computing for Real Time AI","Confirms exact report is a regular technical-session paper rather than a poster."]]}
{"id":"R0130","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"F","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E3","secondary":["E4"],"reason":"Models only generic indivisible IoT computation offloading with multi-agent DRL as optimizer and evaluates only DRL rewards and generic task service delay, with no DNN inference workload or inference evaluation.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"Abstract","introduces a multi-agent-based offloading decision and resource allocation","Presents a primary research contribution; chapter label is container format only."],["E2","PDF",1,"Abstract","multiple UAV-assisted mobile edge computing servers (U-ESs), and","Models and simulates multiple UAV edge servers (N=2) serving ground IoT devices."],["E3","PDF",4,"3.1 Edge Intelligent Digital Twin-Assisted Low-altitude Network","generate a single computation-sensitive task, which cannot be","Checked Sections 3–5: models generic indivisible bit/cycle tasks offloaded to nearest U-ES with DRL used only as optimizer and no DNN inference workload."],["E4","PDF",11,"5 Simulation Results and Analysis","total service delay increases with the number of","Checked Section 5: evaluates only DRL average episode rewards and generic task service delay with no inference method evaluated."],["E5","Codex-supplied",0,"Springer Crossref deposit","online date in the Springer Crossref deposit is 2026-09-20","Authoritative online release date 2026-09-20 is within 2021-01-01 to 2026-11-26, superseding 2027 imprint year."],["E6","PDF",1,"Abstract","With the rapid expansion of smart services in","Full 14-page report is written in English."],["E7","Codex-supplied",0,"https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-032-39125-4","Springer identifies the volume as refereed conference proceedings","Springer URL was inaccessible; Codex-supplied metadata confirms refereed conference proceedings paired with PDF page 1 MONAMI 2025 LNICST 715 identity."],["E7","PDF",1,"Footer","K. Yu et al. (Eds.): MONAMI 2025, LNICST","Matches exact proceedings volume and chapter DOI 10.1007/978-3-032-39125-4_4."]]}
